def minOperations(word: str) -> int:
    n = len(word)
    if n == 0:
        return 0
    INF = float('inf')
    dp = [[INF] * 26 for _ in range(n)]
    for c in range(26):
        cost = 0 if ord(word[0]) - ord('a') == c else 1
        dp[0][c] = cost
    for i in range(1, n):
        for c in range(26):
            cost = 0 if ord(word[i]) - ord('a') == c else 1
            min_prev = INF
            for p in range(26):
                if abs(p - c) > 1:
                    min_prev = min(min_prev, dp[i-1][p])
            dp[i][c] = cost + min_prev
    return min(dp[n-1])
```
The function implements a dynamic programming approach to compute the minimum changes required. It tracks the minimum cost to form a valid prefix ending with each possible character (0-25), ensuring adjacent characters satisfy |diff| > 1. The final answer is the minimum value over all possible endings at the last position. This correctly handles all constraints and examples with O(n * 26 * 26) time.

